From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] wordcraft: zip 9 (RUSTSEC-2026-0545, -0548)

zip 3.0.0 to 9 (owner decision 2026-11-22): the workspace requirement, and the call sites of the one API change
we meet (ZipFile::name and ZipArchive::file_names now return ZipResult<Cow<str>>). Production: package.rs maps a
name error to DocxError::Zip. Tests: .unwrap(). zip 9 fails a read once an entry passes the size its central
directory declares: odt pictures_over_the_budget_are_not_inflated now expects such an entry to cost nothing, and
package part_inflating_past_its_declared_size_is_skipped pins the docx side. Cargo.lock is patch 0921.
---
diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index 3cba5301..b70edafd 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@ vello_cpu = "0.2"
 image = { version = "0.25", default-features = false, features = ["png", "jpeg", "webp", "gif", "bmp", "tiff"] }
 craft-pdf = { git = "https://github.com/storytold/craft-libs", rev = "c3487320b2d1de657b860b3c8abb44e1f2b32bd8", version = "=0.1.0", default-features = false, features = ["write"] }
 quick-xml = "0.41"
-zip = { version = "3", default-features = false, features = ["deflate"] }
+zip = { version = "9", default-features = false, features = ["deflate"] }
 # zlib streams (compressed metafile pictures in `.doc` drawings); already in the lock as a dependency of other crates.
 miniz_oxide = "0.8"
 cfb = "0.15"
